msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32126"
msgid "Automatically sync watch history and ratings"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32127"
msgid "Periodically reconciles resume position, fully-watched status, and rating for every movie, TV show, and episode already in this device's own library against Chronicle, in both directions where applicable (Chronicle's rating always wins; resume/watched use whichever side changed most recently). Lightweight and non-destructive -- never touches any local file, so every device can run it independently on its own schedule with no risk of racing another device. On by default."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32128"
msgid "Sync once shortly after Kodi starts"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32129"
msgid "Runs one sync pass a short while after this device's Chronicle Scraper service starts (e.g. after a Kodi restart), in addition to the regular interval below. On by default."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32130"
msgid "Sync every (minutes)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32131"
msgid "How often the automatic background sync runs, in 30-minute steps. Defaults to every 2 hours (120 minutes)."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32132"
msgid "Sync Watch History and Ratings Now"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32133"
msgid "Runs one sync pass immediately, regardless of the automatic settings above. Useful right after changing something in Chronicle you want reflected in Kodi without waiting for the next scheduled sync."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32134"
msgid "Syncing watch history and ratings…"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32135"
msgid "Synced {0} movie(s), {1} show(s), {2} episode(s){3}"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32136"
msgid " -- {0} error(s), see kodi.log"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32137"
msgid "New Content Detection"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32138"
msgid "Periodically check for new content"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32139"
msgid "Chronicle can tell this device when new movies/TV content has been imported that Kodi hasn't discovered yet (VideoLibrary.Refresh, used everywhere else, only works on an item Kodi already has -- discovering a brand-new file needs a real library scan). This device always checks once when Kodi starts, regardless of this setting. Turning this on also checks periodically while Kodi keeps running, at the interval below -- off by default, since most imports happen on Chronicle's own nightly schedule and are already caught by the next Kodi startup. Only ever scans the source folder(s) this addon is actually the configured scraper for on this device, never anything else."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32140"
msgid "Check every (minutes)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32141"
msgid "How often the periodic check runs, in 30-minute steps. Defaults to every 2 hours (120 minutes)."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32142"
msgid "Collection Art"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32143"
msgid "Syncing collection art…"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32144"
msgid "Automatically sync collection art"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32145"
msgid "Periodically refreshes every collection's poster/fanart/logo/etc. in Kodi's own \"Movie set information folder\" from Chronicle -- not just the collections that happen to get touched as a side effect of one of their member movies being rescraped. Replaces Chronicle_Scrobbler's own collection art sync, which pushed the same art a different way (directly via Kodi's API instead of into this dedicated folder) -- movie collections belong entirely to this addon now. On by default."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32146"
msgid "Sync Collection Art Now"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32147"
msgid "Synced {0} collection(s){1}"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32148"
msgid "Runs one collection art sync pass immediately, regardless of the automatic settings above. Useful right after changing a collection's art in Chronicle you want reflected in Kodi without waiting for the next scheduled sync."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32149"
msgid "Verify every movie matches Chronicle after each scan"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32150"
msgid "After any video library scan finishes -- Kodi's own automatic one, your own manual \"Update Library\", or this addon's own new-content detection above -- checks every movie Kodi already has against Chronicle's current data (matched by the exact video file, not by title/year) and corrects only whatever actually disagrees. Fixes cases where a file was scraped with the wrong data at some point and never corrected since. On by default."
msgstr ""
